bak/

BC.History/

.mcp.json

# tree-harness parse-tree snapshots (regenerated locally; large)
.snapshots/

# tools/query_coverage/ is a checked-in package (query-coverage test harness),
# not scratch — unignore its .py files despite the blanket *.py rule above,
# and its reports/ output dir and __pycache__ dirs stay ignored.
!tools/query_coverage/**/*.py
tools/query_coverage/**/__pycache__/
tools/query_coverage/reports/

# tools/precedence/ is the operator-precedence probe rig — the acceptance
# instrument for every relation in the expression ladder, not scratch. Its
# cases/*.al ARE the probes, so they must survive the blanket *.al rule the same
# way query_coverage's .py files survive the blanket *.py rule. Without these
# two lines the rig commits as a README and a .tsv describing 196 files that are
# not there, which is worse than not committing it at all.
!tools/precedence/**/*.py
!tools/precedence/cases/*.al
tools/precedence/**/__pycache__/
